#!/bin/bash

# omarchy:summary=Explain how to restore the default tmux config on NixOS.

# Upstream copies the shipped tmux.conf over the user's. That cannot work here:
# ~/.config/tmux/tmux.conf is a read-only symlink into the nix store, written by
# programs.tmux.extraConfig. There is no user copy to overwrite -- and copying
# over the symlink would replace it with a plain file that home-manager then
# collides with on the next rebuild.
#
# So this explains the model rather than pretending to perform the operation.

set -euo pipefail

cat <<'MESSAGE'
Your tmux config comes from your flake, not from a file you edit here.

  ~/.config/tmux/tmux.conf is a read-only link into the nix store,
  generated from programs.tmux.extraConfig.

It is already the shipped default, so there is nothing to restore. To
change it, edit the source and rebuild:

  config/tmux/tmux.conf        in your omarchy-nix checkout
  sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake <your-flake>

To add settings without forking omarchy-nix, set programs.tmux.extraConfig
in your own home-manager configuration; it merges with the shipped config.
MESSAGE
